  "question": {
    "text": "Taking <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>X</mi></math>-axis along horizontal and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>Y</mi></math>-axis along vertical, with what minimum speed must a particle be projected from the origin so that it is able to pass through a given point <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>(</mo><mn>30</mn><mo>&nbsp;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi><mo>,</mo><mo>&nbsp;</mo><mn>40</mn><mo>&nbsp;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi><mo>)</mo></math>? Take <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>g</mi><mo>&nbsp;</mo><mo>=</mo><mo>&nbsp;</mo><mn>10</mn><mo>&nbsp;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi><mo>&nbsp;</mo><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">s</mi><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup></math>"
  },
